msgid "Suppression List"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1134
msgid "Opted-out addresses, one per line. These never receive non-transactional e-mails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1147
msgid "Send Log"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1148
msgid "Keep a log of sent e-mails (recipient, subject, status — no message content)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1161
msgid "Confirmation Window (hours)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1162
msgid "Unconfirmed subscriptions are deleted after this many hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1172
msgid "Retention (days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1173
msgid "Completed/unsubscribed records are deleted after this many days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1183
msgid "Store Consent IP"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1184
msgid "Also store the IP address as part of the consent record (optional)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1204
msgid "Privacy Policy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1205
msgid "A suggestion for the MixMyMeals section of your privacy policy, generated from the settings in the other tabs. It changes by itself when they do — check your published policy after changing a retention period or switching a feature on or off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1209
msgid "WordPress emoji"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1210
msgid "Do not load WordPress's emoji script and emoji images from WordPress’s own servers (WordPress Foundation, USA). Browsers show emoji themselves; switched off, the site makes no request to a third party for them and the privacy policy needs no section on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1248
msgid "Nutrition tables"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1249
msgid "Choose which columns the table shows and what they are called. Leave a heading empty for the default wording. Style the table in your child theme through .mmm-nutri-table."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1283
#: includes/lib/class-mixmymeals-shortcodes.php:2901
msgid "Traffic light per 100 g"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1284
msgid "Rates fat, saturates, sugars and salt per 100 g as low, medium or high on ingredients, recipes, meals and plans; empty both fields of a figure to switch its light off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1293
msgid "Preset with the UK Food Standards Agency's values; change them only if you follow another scheme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1295
msgid "Off by default: per 100 g this figure says little about a healthy diet, which is what the plan rating covers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1302
#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1358
#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1392
msgid "kcal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1302
#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1358
#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1392
msgid "g"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1313
msgid "High per serving above"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1314
msgid "On recipes and meals, a serving providing more than this share of the reference intake of fat, saturates, sugars or salt turns that light red; empty switches the rule off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1336
msgid "Reference intake"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1337
msgid "What one day should hold, the basis of every percentage: in the nutrition tables, the tiles and bars, the plan rating, mails and the PDF. Empty fields use the EU reference intake of an average adult. Set your own only for an audience whose needs differ; the notes under the tables then name your energy figure instead of the average adult."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1345
msgid "Maximum per day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1348
msgid "Target per day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1351
msgid "Reference per day."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: name of a profile of the people on a plan, e.g. "Child".
#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1383
#, php-format
msgid "Reference intake: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1384
msgid "For people on a plan with this profile. Empty fields use the figure above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1415
msgid "Plan rating"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1416
msgid "Rates a plan's average per day and person against the reference intake of an average adult, beside the percentages in the plan's nutrition table and in the planner."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1426
msgid "\"Too much\" shows whenever the day's average goes above this; raise it only for an audience with higher needs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1428
msgid "\"Too little\" shows below this, and only when every planned day has breakfast, lunch and dinner; lower it for light eaters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1430
msgid "Too much above the first value, too little below the second (only for whole days); empty either to leave it out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1476
msgid "Chips"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1477
msgid "The small labels on recipes, meals, plans and archive cards. Leave a field empty for the wording of the site language. Placeholders in curly braces are filled in; a pattern that drops the value the chip exists to state is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1521
msgid "Terms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1522
msgid "Single words that appear in several places. Leave a field empty for the wording of the site language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1526
msgid "Recipe as written"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1527
msgid "The first diet choice of a meal whose recipe can be cooked several ways: the recipe with its own products. Shown in the planner, the \"Plan this recipe as a meal\" dialog, the Meals box and on the meal screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mixmymeals-settings.php:1534
msgid "Language"
